# Proposal: Gallery MCP Write Surface (pointer moves)

Status: PROPOSAL — needs Joel sign-off before any auth is implemented.
Authored: 2026-09-14 · maker pass, following the live hot-swap proof
(ledger row `gallery-hotswap-825011b`).

## What exists now (verified)

- `content/current.json` in the Archive R2 bucket is the gallery's runtime
  pointer. The page boots from it (through `cinema.wzrrd.sh/archive/*`)
  and hot-swaps studies in an already-open tab within one 60s poll —
  proven with o11y receipts: `gallery.study.swapped` →
  `study.scene.live`, no reload, no redeploy.
- Pointer moves currently happen through the maker's agent-secrets REST
  path (operator-side). That is not a durable write surface; it is a
  manual capability that happens to work.

## What is proposed

One Worker endpoint on the existing `cinema.wzrrd.sh` worker surface:

- `PUT /mcp/content/current` — body is exactly the pointer document
  (`{ study, sha, updatedAt, url, archive }`), validated before write.
- Writes ONLY the key `archive/content/current.json` via the existing
  `ARCHIVE` R2 binding. Cannot touch study bundles, manifests, or the
  SPA assets. Scope is one key, by construction.
- Auth: Cloudflare service token (account-scoped API token minted with
  Workers + R2 edit on this one bucket only), checked against
  `cf-ray`-signed header `CF-Access-Client-Id` (or a static bearer in a
  Worker secret, if that tests simpler first pass). Reject everything
  else with 401 + o11y failure event.
- Every call logs an o11y event: caller id, old pointer, new pointer,
  result. Read path (gallery.study.swapped) already logs the effect.

## Why the gate matters

VISION.md names the MCP write surface "a publishing capability on a
public site… treated like one". This proposal keeps that boundary:
- Content still reaches viewers only as validated pointer documents.
- The endpoint cannot read private state, cannot mutate studies, and
  cannot publish anything beyond what the archive route already serves.
- Worst case for a leaked token: someone moves the gallery pointer to
  an archived, already-shipped study. No new surface, no arbitrary
  content, no assets touched.

## What changes for the maker loop

Today: study verified → archive-ship → upload → curl 200 → ledger →
ShitRat. The pointer move is a manual REST call in the same pane.

After sign-off: same chain, but the final step is one authenticated
`PUT /mcp/content/current` — so any joelclaw surface (shitrAM, a
scheduled producer, a fresh session) can move the gallery without
holding Cloudflare account credentials. The 20-day producer (queue
item 4) depends on this being durable rather than manual.

## Not in this proposal

- A generic content API (no arbitrary key writes, ever).
- Public run history (VISION will-not).
- Scheduling the producer (chain item D; blocked on sign-off AND on
  this surface existing).
